            "note": "SF-0009 closes the merge-loss path of HAZ-0001 that SF-0001 (integrity hash) cannot detect: a lossy git merge of project.req yields an internally-consistent, correctly-hashed file that is simply missing one side's safety requirements. By making the merge driver fail safe (auto-merge the reconcilable, surface any unresolvable divergence as a conflict, never silently pick a side — SR-0010), a safety requirement can no longer be silently lost across a merge. SF-0009 is realized by SR-0010 (awaiting human co-sign).",
