      "description": "Tool-confidence hazard (IEC 61508-3 §7.4.4). req tracks only the REQUIRED/allocated/inherited integrity TARGET and the verified links between artifacts; it does not track ACHIEVED integrity (PFDavg/PFH, HFT/SFF architectural constraints, diagnostic coverage, systematic capability). The §3A-3 misread the review flagged as the most dangerous: a green trace read as proof the realized system meets its target failure measure. SIL3 policy allocation, consistent with the other tool-confidence hazards.",
      "frequency": "F_B",
      "harm": "A user reads a fully-linked, Verified req trace as proof the realized system achieves its integrity target, when req records nothing about achieved integrity; unsubstantiated achieved-integrity ships on the strength of a green traceability spine.",
