      "id": "REQ-0023",
      "kind": "Functional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Should",
      "rationale": "A pre-commit hook is the cheapest place to catch conformance errors before they reach review, and one command to install removes a per-developer setup chore.",
      "statement": "The system shall manage a project-local pre-commit hook running `req conform` on staged `.req` files via `req hooks install` and `req hooks uninstall`.",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [
        "integration",
        "git"
      ],
