      "title": "Resolve ID collisions after merge via req renumber",
      "updated": "2026-06-15T07:06:28.816291200Z",
      "verification": {
        "actor": "sonnet-verify-run",
        "analysis": {
          "actor": "sonnet-verify-run",
          "at": "2026-06-15T07:06:25.636949100Z",
          "outcome": "Pass",
          "references": [
            "E:\\Development\\cli_req\\src\\commands\\renumber.rs"
          ],
          "summary": "AC1 (no remaining duplicates): plan_renames() at renumber.rs:143-164 detects collisions by comparing created() + title() between current and base artifacts; mismatched pairs are assigned fresh IDs via the per-family counter; rekey() at lines 166-174 removes the old key and inserts under the new one, eliminating the duplicate.\n\nAC2 (links rewritten): rewrite_links() at lines 178-189 iterates all link targets for every artifact family and substitutes new IDs from the combined HashMap built at line 121; called at lines 122-125 for requirements, hazards, safety functions, and safety requirements.\n\nAC3 (history entry recording old ID): note_renamed() in the Artifact trait macro (lines 41-45) pushes a history entry formatted as \"renumbered from {old} (merge with base)\". Invoked inside rekey() at line 170 (a.note_renamed(old)).\n\nAC4 (--dry-run prints without writing): Lines 105-111 print planned renames unconditionally, then check args.dry_run and return Ok(()) before the storage::save() call at line 131."
        },
