      "id": "REQ-0094",
      "kind": "Functional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Could",
      "rationale": "Agents and humans paste capitalised forms because that's how they appear in `req show`. The current case-sensitive rejection produces a clap tip that names the alternative but feels like a tool quirk rather than a design choice.",
      "statement": "The CLI shall accept status values in any case (`Implemented`, `implemented`, `IMPLEMENTED`) and normalise to the canonical lowercase form before the conformance check.",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [
        "ux",
        "ergonomics",
        "agents"
      ],
