      "id": "REQ-0095",
      "kind": "Functional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Could",
      "rationale": "A common mistake is to soft-delete a requirement and immediately re-add it instead of editing the original. The result is a broken audit trail and orphaned history. Surfacing the duplicate intent at add time preserves the link to the prior conversation.",
      "statement": "The CLI shall warn when `req add` would create a requirement whose title is highly similar to a requirement that was moved to Obsolete within the last 60 days, suggesting `req update` or `req split --keep-original` as alternatives.",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [
        "history",
        "ux",
        "conformance"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "actor": "Tom",
          "at": "2026-05-18T07:41:35.967483500Z",
          "commit": "541ced677545eef8ec9fbac5c4b1f6ff8bc3b13d",
          "kind": "Inspection",
          "notes": "Implementation in src/ with REQ-NNNN marker; regression tests in tests/",
          "outcome": "Pass"
        },
        {
          "actor": "Tom",
          "at": "2026-06-12T22:11:27.729202200Z",
          "commit": "7107cab238bf327eab0eb41a18956905b38e8d93",
          "content_hash": "aa58a39e48a0a31e36d2ad1411682c363226b76dce07ca9d38a15b2d35466e05",
          "kind": "Inspection",
          "linked_files": [
            ".\\CHANGELOG.md",
            ".\\src\\commands\\add.rs"
          ],
          "notes": "validation dossier concluded — Verified implementation in src/commands/add.rs; code uses Jaccard token similarity on tokens to detect new requirements similar to those retired (Obsolete) within 60 days, preventing history loss by flagging high-similarity matches.",
          "outcome": "Pass"
        },
        {
          "actor": "Tom",
          "at": "2026-06-13T06:09:35.553160300Z",
          "commit": "7107cab238bf327eab0eb41a18956905b38e8d93",
