      "id": "REQ-0097",
      "kind": "NonFunctional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Could",
      "rationale": "Sequential per-requirement hook calls scale linearly with project size; a 200-req project with a 1s hook is 200s of conformance checking. Bounded parallelism is the natural answer but needs a deliberate design — concurrency cap (CLI flag vs env var), batched stdin (one call per N reqs), and ordering guarantees in the output.",
      "statement": "The conformance checker shall offer a bounded-concurrency mode for the LLM hook so that N requirements can be evaluated in parallel up to a configurable cap, with stable ordering of findings in the final report.",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [
        "performance",
        "design",
        "conformance"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "actor": "Tom",
          "at": "2026-05-18T07:41:36.742150500Z",
