      "id": "REQ-0119",
      "kind": "Functional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Should",
      "rationale": "Confirmed during 0.4.0-rc.1 E2E testing: req import accepts a payload whose schema declares rationale optional, then the conformance checker rejects it for missing rationale. A schema that says 'this field is optional' must be honoured by the conformance checker or the schema is lying. Fix is either to make rationale required in the import schema (preferred, matches the rest of the conformance checker's contract) or to relax the conformance checker for imported content (worse, weakens the spec).",
      "statement": "The import JSON schema shall declare rationale as required so the schema and the conformance checker agree on which fields are mandatory.",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [
        "bugfix",
        "import",
        "schema"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "actor": "Tom",
          "at": "2026-05-20T12:25:17.277567500Z",
