      "id": "REQ-0130",
      "kind": "Functional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Should",
      "rationale": "A Verified requirement with a failing latest test record is the spec asserting a falsehood about the world — it claims the behaviour works, while the most recent evidence says it does not. Surfacing this in `req conform` puts the signal in CI logs, pre-commit output, and MCP responses without breaking active development (which often involves a known-failing record while a fix is in flight). The hard block stays in `req review --gate --no-defects` (REQ-0126); this requirement is the soft, ever-present signal. Distinct from REQ-0125 because that adds the count to status/brief/lint; this adds it to the conformance findings stream where every consumer already pays attention.",
      "statement": "The conformance checker shall emit a REQ-V-0024 warning on any requirement whose status is Verified and whose latest test record has a Fail outcome, so the structural contradiction surfaces in every `req conform` call without flipping the exit code.",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [
        "polish",
        "conformance"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "actor": "Tom",
          "at": "2026-05-21T15:56:50.950000500Z",
          "commit": "8a02b3b5f1f43c42467aa92213f49c4492d8c305",
          "kind": "Composition",
          "notes": "cites: req_0130_validate_warns_on_verified_with_failing_latest, req_0130_validate_does_not_fail_on_warning_only, req_0130_verified_with_pass_latest_clean — Fires on Verified+failing-latest; doesn't fire on Verified+passing-latest; exit code stays zero.",
          "outcome": "Pass"
        },
        {
