      "id": "REQ-0140",
      "kind": "Functional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Must",
      "rationale": "An older req binary (e.g. a stale MCP server) deserialises project.req, drops fields it does not model, and re-serialises without them — silently destroying newer data such as the per-requirement verification dossier. A serde flatten catch-all on each entity makes the loss impossible going forward.",
      "statement": "The storage layer shall round-trip any unrecognised field on a requirement record, the project root, or a safety entity (hazard, safety function, safety requirement) unchanged across a load followed by a save, so a binary that does not model the field does not drop it.",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [],
      "tests": [
        {
          "actor": "Tom",
          "at": "2026-06-12T20:34:37.825740500Z",
          "commit": "7107cab238bf327eab0eb41a18956905b38e8d93",
          "content_hash": "41891dda06eb0645ada902a756c202c569a08340e795258a1e8afdc125085111",
          "kind": "Automated",
          "linked_files": [
            ".\\CHANGELOG.md",
            ".\\src\\commands\\safety.rs",
            ".\\src\\model.rs",
            ".\\src\\storage.rs",
            ".\\tests\\forward_compat.rs"
          ],
          "notes": "cargo test: 1 pass / 0 fail / 0 ignored — req_0140_unknown_requirement_field_round_trips",
