      "id": "REQ-0150",
      "kind": "Functional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Must",
      "rationale": "REQ-0145 makes a human co-sign mandatory for a safety requirement to truly pass, and REQ-V-0034 enforces it in req conform. But the provenance report (SR-0004's HAZ-0002 tool-confidence control) only inspects dossier provenance, so a genuine-but-unconfirmed safety requirement reads as genuine and trustworthy when it is not. Surfacing the missing co-sign keeps the report honest about real verification standing.",
      "statement": "The verification provenance report (req verification report) shall classify a Verified safety requirement that has a genuine passing dossier but no human confirmation as unconfirmed rather than genuine.",
      "status": "Obsolete",
      "tags": [
        "safety",
        "verification"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "actor": "Tom",
          "at": "2026-06-13T19:44:36.422818200Z",
          "commit": "42d3c4c2dc7329207dc842a2f399019176747a51",
          "content_hash": "166261e4e151505221e8e3b7111c5738ad7a475572b1c25aac31682e3e97c723",
