      "title": "Provenance report surfaces human-confirmation status for safety requirements",
      "updated": "2026-06-17T17:41:23.504632300Z",
      "verification": {
        "actor": "Tom",
        "analysis": {
          "actor": "Tom",
          "at": "2026-06-17T17:39:47.311243900Z",
          "outcome": "Pass",
          "references": [
            "src/commands/provenance.rs",
            "src/commands/verification.rs"
          ],
          "summary": "provenance_report() applies an SR-only overlay (src/commands/provenance.rs): a Verified safety requirement whose dossier is genuine but whose human_confirmation is None reclassifies to Unconfirmed, is excluded from the genuine count and surfaced under --not-genuine; the overlay is kept outside classify() so promotion stays gated on classify().is_genuine() before the human co-signs. Behaviour unchanged."
        },
        "concluded": "2026-06-17T17:41:23.504632300Z",
        "concluded_commit": "69c62219a4cd17e520ce2795437540f51c12cb54",
        "opened": "2026-06-17T17:39:46.896732100Z",
