      "id": "REQ-0151",
      "kind": "NonFunctional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Should",
      "rationale": "Several command and flag descriptions were authored as doc-comments beginning with their implementation marker (e.g. 'REQ-0101: project-wide quality audit ...'), which clap renders verbatim into --help. Exposing internal traceability ids in user-facing help is confusing and unprofessional. Implementation markers belong in non-rendered code comments; the help text should read cleanly. Inline examples of the id format (e.g. 'provide an id such as REQ-0007') remain allowed because they help users, and are not marker prefixes.",
      "statement": "The help text rendered by req --help and every subcommand --help shall not contain a requirement, hazard, safety-function, or safety-requirement identifier marker (an id of the form REQ-NNNN, HAZ-NNNN, SF-NNNN, or SR-NNNN immediately followed by a colon).",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [
        "ux",
        "help"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
