      "id": "REQ-0152",
      "kind": "Constraint",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Must",
      "rationale": "hash_files hashed each linked file's raw bytes plus its path string verbatim. A dossier anchored on Windows stored backslash paths and CRLF-sensitive content, so on a Linux/macOS CI checkout the backslash path failed to resolve (file read as empty) and a CRLF checkout hashed differently than an LF one — both falsely reported the safety requirement as stale (REQ-V-0035) and blocked CI on every platform. A staleness anchor must reflect logical source content, not the OS or autocrlf setting of whoever verified it.",
      "statement": "The content hash used to anchor verification and test-record staleness shall be computed identically on every host platform, regardless of local path-separator or line-ending conventions.",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [
        "forward-compat",
        "storage",
        "verification"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "actor": "Tom",
          "at": "2026-06-13T20:32:50.604973200Z",
          "commit": "7aa9e5c47c02bcd25f21e4701a85350a440790d5",
          "content_hash": "8ab355c08ccb3d540b67c0a9a202cd6ae72cac55276ed2781b2bd8288d974ba8",
          "kind": "Inspection",
          "linked_files": [
            "./src/commands/test_cmd.rs",
            "./src/commands/validation.rs"
          ],
          "notes": "validation dossier concluded — REQ-0152 met: the staleness content hash is computed identically on every platform -- path separators normalized to forward slash, carriage returns stripped -- so a dossier anchored on one OS is not falsely stale on another. Backed by code review and the req_0152 unit test.",
          "outcome": "Pass"
        },
        {
          "actor": "Tom",
          "at": "2026-06-13T21:06:53.237991900Z",
          "commit": "7aa9e5c47c02bcd25f21e4701a85350a440790d5",
          "content_hash": "214b63b7bfe691e1ca564a0d482239ff478a087a51a62d1a5653349bca981d39",
          "kind": "Inspection",
          "linked_files": [
