      "id": "REQ-0153",
      "kind": "Functional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Should",
      "rationale": "A hash-format change (REQ-0152) makes every stored content hash stale at once, even for sources that never changed. Re-verifying those by hand would be enormous busywork, but blindly rehashing all of them would mask genuine drift and defeat the staleness guard. A targeted command compares the legacy hash of the current source to the stored hash: a match proves the bytes are identical to the anchor, so the new normalized hash can be substituted without re-verification; a mismatch is left stale for real re-verification. Safety requirements are never auto-refreshed, preserving the human re-anchor and co-sign requirement.",
      "statement": "The tool shall provide a command that re-normalizes a dossier's staleness content hash only when the source is cryptographically proven unchanged since the anchor, leaving genuinely-drifted dossiers stale.",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [
        "forward-compat",
        "verification"
      ],
