      "id": "REQ-0154",
      "kind": "Functional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Must",
      "rationale": "SILs are derived lazily on read from the hazard risk-graph parameters and the project calibration, so a later calibration change or a newly-linked higher-SIL hazard silently moves a safety requirement's effective SIL away from the integrity level its evidence was actually justified against. Without a recorded snapshot there is no way to detect that drift or to know which SIL a past verification was performed under, which is the single most dangerous silent state in the safety layer today.",
      "statement": "The tool shall record, on each safety-requirement verification record, the SIL value that was in effect for that requirement at the moment the evidence was captured.",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [
        "safety-impact",
        "safety"
      ],
