      "id": "REQ-0155",
      "kind": "Functional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Must",
      "rationale": "Snapshotting the SIL at verification time is only useful if escalation is detected. When a higher-SIL hazard is later linked to a safety function, every downstream safety requirement inherits the raised SIL while its evidence still reflects the old, weaker integrity target, and nothing surfaces the mismatch until someone happens to re-verify. Making this a hard conformance error forces re-verification before the chain can be considered sound again.",
      "statement": "The conformance checker shall raise an error when a safety requirement's current inherited SIL is higher than the SIL recorded on its most recent passing verification evidence.",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [
        "safety-impact",
        "safety"
      ],
