      "id": "REQ-0158",
      "kind": "Functional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Must",
      "rationale": "Ordinary requirements enforce the lifecycle ladder through is_natural_transition, but safety requirements currently bypass that guard, so a Verified safety requirement can be demoted with no force flag at all. This gives the most safety-critical artifacts weaker lifecycle discipline than ordinary ones, which is exactly backwards.",
      "statement": "The tool shall reject a safety-requirement status transition that is not a natural lifecycle step unless the caller supplies a force flag together with a reason.",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [
        "safety-lifecycle",
        "safety"
      ],
