      "id": "REQ-0160",
      "kind": "Functional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Should",
      "rationale": "A complete trace means the hazard-to-evidence chain is linked and each link is verified, not that the mitigation actually reduces residual risk to an acceptable level. A reader who sees the word complete will infer a safety-adequacy claim the tool deliberately does not make, so the output must state its own scope.",
      "statement": "The trace command shall label a fully-linked chain as linked and verified rather than presenting wording that implies the residual risk has been validated as acceptable.",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [
        "safety-lifecycle",
        "safety"
      ],
