      "id": "REQ-0162",
      "kind": "Functional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Should",
      "rationale": "Dossier provenance is currently classified by testing whether the plan string starts with a magic marker, which is fragile and survives a confirmed direct edit of the prefix. Persisting the exemption type as an explicit enumerated field makes provenance classification robust and tamper-evident under the integrity hash.",
      "statement": "The tool shall store the exemption type of a verification dossier as an enumerated field rather than inferring it from a prefix of the free-text plan.",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [
        "evidence"
      ],
