      "id": "REQ-0164",
      "kind": "Functional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Should",
      "rationale": "Conformance rule codes such as REQ-V-0010 are currently buried inside prose error strings, so an agent cannot branch on the specific failure without brittle substring parsing. Exposing the code as its own field lets an agent route each failure class deterministically and look up the matching guidance.",
      "statement": "The MCP server shall return the conformance rule code as a discrete field on every rejection rather than only embedding it in the human-readable message.",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [
        "agent-surface"
      ],
