      "priority": "Should",
      "rationale": "Dependency cycles are caught only during the full req conform sweep today, so an agent discovers the broken graph several commits after creating it. Rejecting the closing edge at link time keeps the failure adjacent to the action that caused it, which is far cheaper to fix.",
      "statement": "The link command shall reject a depends-on edge that would close a cycle in the dependency graph.",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [
        "agent-surface"
      ],
