      "id": "REQ-0168",
      "kind": "Functional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Could",
      "rationale": "IEC 61508 independence of assessment is not representable today, so a single actor can author, realize, and verify an entire safety chain unchallenged. A warning when author and verifier coincide is a cheap first step toward an independence argument without yet modelling the full competence and independence matrix.",
      "statement": "The conformance checker shall warn when the actor who verified a safety requirement is the same actor who authored it.",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [
        "attribution",
        "safety"
      ],
