      "id": "REQ-0171",
      "kind": "Functional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Should",
      "rationale": "An acknowledgement is evidence in its own right and must be anchored to the state of the code it was made against, so that a later change to the chain can be detected as invalidating the prior review. Capturing reviewer, time, and commit places the acknowledgement on the same commit join key the rest of the evidence model uses.",
      "statement": "The tool shall record each safety-walkthrough acknowledgement with the reviewer identity, the timestamp, and the commit at which the review was performed.",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [
        "guided-review",
        "safety"
      ],
