      "id": "REQ-0174",
      "kind": "Functional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Should",
      "rationale": "A reviewer cannot meaningfully accept a requirement whose supporting chain is incomplete, and allowing acknowledgement of a broken chain would launder a gap into an apparent sign-off. Refusing acknowledgement until the chain is whole keeps the walkthrough honest about what has actually been demonstrated.",
      "statement": "The guided safety walkthrough shall prevent acknowledgement of any safety requirement whose chain is missing a hazard assessment, a mitigating safety function, or passing verification evidence.",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [
        "guided-review",
        "safety"
      ],
