      "id": "REQ-0184",
      "kind": "Functional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Should",
      "rationale": "Safety verification is human-gated by design through the co-sign and guided-walkthrough requirements, and an automated test bench, however trustworthy, must not be able to satisfy that gate unattended. Ordinary requirements may reach Verified on ingested evidence, but a safety requirement may only accumulate that evidence pending the human confirmation its integrity level demands.",
      "statement": "The tool shall refuse to promote a safety requirement to Verified solely on the basis of externally-ingested evidence.",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [
        "test-integration",
        "at-test",
        "safety"
      ],
