      "id": "REQ-0186",
      "kind": "Functional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Should",
      "rationale": "The vague-term rule currently flags the substring etc inside legitimate words such as fetches, producing false positives that force an author to reword a perfectly clear statement. Matching on word boundaries removes the false positives without weakening detection of the genuine vague terms the rule exists to catch.",
      "statement": "The conformance checker shall apply its vague-term and weasel-word checks on whole-word boundaries rather than as substring matches.",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [
        "lint",
        "conformance"
      ],
      "tests": [
