      "id": "REQ-0188",
      "kind": "Functional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Must",
      "rationale": "The dangerous failure is a half-verified safety requirement that is invisible (omitted because it is not Verified) or that silently reads as done. Either way a reviewer believes the safety case is finished when no human has signed off. The awaiting-confirmation state must be loud at every gate and report.",
      "statement": "A safety requirement that is not genuinely done (no dossier, failing dossier, awaiting human co-sign, or stale) shall be surfaced as not-yet-complete in the verification report, req conform output, hazard trace, and safety-requirement listings, and shall never be counted as complete nor omitted from any of them.",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [
        "safety",
        "verification"
      ],
