      "id": "REQ-0189",
      "kind": "Functional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Must",
      "rationale": "req trace reports a hazard safety case complete true from status alone, while req conform reports hard errors on the same requirements when they are unconfirmed or stale. One view says the safety case is finished, the other says it is not. Completeness must be defined as conform-clean so the tool cannot simultaneously claim done and not-done.",
      "statement": "The hazard safety-case completeness computed by req trace and assessment shall count a realizing safety requirement as satisfied only when the conformance checker also considers it done, meaning genuinely verified, human-confirmed, and not stale, so the two views never contradict.",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [
        "safety",
        "verification"
      ],
