      "id": "REQ-0193",
      "kind": "Functional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Must",
      "rationale": "req safety accept conflated three jobs — enabling the feature, accepting the liability disclaimer, and (via REQ-0172) signing off the safety case — so enabling the feature depended circularly on a case that can only be built once it is enabled. Naming the activation command accept-disclaimer and decoupling it from acknowledgement removes the circularity; the acknowledgement gate belongs on the sign-off check.",
      "statement": "Activating the functional-safety features by accepting the disclaimer shall be a distinctly-named command whose success is never gated on safety-requirement acknowledgement.",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [
        "safety",
        "verification"
      ],
      "tests": [
