      "id": "REQ-0200",
      "kind": "Functional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Should",
      "rationale": "After a refactor that touches shared files, many genuine dossiers go stale on a whole-file hash even though behaviour is unchanged. Re-running the agent review to re-confirm is wasteful; a passing acceptance test at HEAD is objective evidence that the requirement is still met, so it can re-anchor the dossier cheaply and honestly without a model rubber-stamp.",
      "statement": "req shall provide a command that re-anchors a stale ordinary requirement's verification dossier to the current commit when its automated tests pass, recording the test run as the evidence.",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [
        "verification"
      ],
