      "id": "REQ-0204",
      "kind": "Functional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Should",
      "rationale": "The 61508 review's lopsided-rigour finding extends down the chain: a parent (hazard or SF) must not be argued adequately covered while a child (its SFs, or their SRs) is unaddressed or unverified. Forcing a per-child note and hard-gating on the children's Verified state makes sign-off proceed bottom-up and turns the bare mitigates/realizes edge into recorded reasoning.",
      "statement": "req shall refuse to conclude a safety function's or hazard's adequacy dossier until every live child it decomposes into is addressed by a walk-through note and is itself Verified.",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [],
      "tests": [
