      "id": "REQ-0207",
      "kind": "Functional",
      "links": [],
      "priority": "Must",
      "rationale": "The previous merge driver ('req renumber --base %O || true') was misconfigured (renumber expects a git ref, not git's %O temp-file path) and the trailing '|| true' swallowed the failure, so git silently kept one side wholesale — observed dropping an entire branch's safety model during the rc.6 integration. A real semantic merge that fails loud on genuine conflict is required so spec data is never silently lost on merge.",
      "statement": "req shall provide a 'req merge' command usable as a git merge driver that performs a three-way merge of two divergent project.req versions against their common ancestor. It shall auto-merge all non-conflicting changes from both sides — additions, deletions, and edits to distinct artifacts or distinct fields — and write the reconciled, re-signed spec on success (exit 0). When a change cannot be unambiguously reconciled (the same artifact or field edited differently on both sides, or an edit-versus-delete), it shall NOT choose a side silently: it shall preserve both versions and exit non-zero so the merge surfaces as a conflict for human resolution. 'req hooks' and 'req doctor' shall register this driver and shall not mask its exit status (no '|| true').",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [],
      "tests": [
        {
          "actor": "Tom",
          "at": "2026-06-17T15:36:20.551870200Z",
          "commit": "bfea77f95a4021f0b8402fcdab167a86ea06e22a",
          "content_hash": "f71cca0dc98e17a12c281142e54037761c458db284c9a7b0bcea45ef6d57c252",
          "kind": "Inspection",
          "linked_files": [
            "./src/cli.rs",
            "./src/commands/doctor.rs",
            "./src/commands/hooks.rs",
            "./src/commands/merge.rs",
            "./src/main.rs",
            "./src/storage.rs",
            "./tests/merge.rs"
          ],
          "notes": "verification dossier concluded — req merge performs a semantic three-way merge of project.req: non-conflicting changes from both sides (additions with collision-renumber, deletions, and edits to distinct artifacts/fields) are auto-merged and the result re-signed; any unresolvable divergence preserves both sides and exits non-zero as a git conflict. req hooks and req doctor register this driver without masking its exit status. Verified by code review and the req_0207_* integration tests.",
          "outcome": "Pass"
        },
        {
          "actor": "Tom",
          "at": "2026-06-17T15:53:52.756122200Z",
