      "safe_state": "No spec mutation is accepted from a merge that cannot be unambiguously reconciled; the divergence is held as a conflict pending human resolution.",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [],
      "title": "Spec merges fail safe — divergent merges surface as conflicts, never silent overwrite",
      "updated": "2026-06-19T20:06:16.312384600Z",
      "verification": {
        "actor": "Tom",
        "analysis": {
          "actor": "Tom",
          "at": "2026-06-17T15:38:01.678915Z",
          "outcome": "Pass",
          "references": [
            "src/commands/merge.rs",
            "SR-0010"
          ],
          "summary": "SF-0009 is realized solely by SR-0010. SR-0010 mandates exactly the fail-safe behaviour the function names: a semantic 3-way merge that preserves every artifact from either side, renumbers colliding additions (keeping both), and on any unresolvable divergence preserves both sides and exits non-zero. The implementation (src/commands/merge.rs) and its registration (hooks.rs/doctor.rs, no '|| true') were reviewed under SR-0010. No residual fail-open path: the only silent side-picks are where the other side made no change relative to the base."
        },
        "chain_anchor": "SR-0010:v:b157693e3d4e",
        "concluded": "2026-06-19T20:03:19.446084200Z",
