      "id": "SR-0005",
      "links": [
        {
          "kind": "Realizes",
          "target": "SF-0005"
        }
      ],
      "priority": "Must",
      "rationale": "The word validate is currently bound to a consistency linter while the real V&V workflow lands in Verified, so the tool contradicts the standards it supports and misleads users about safety-case state (HAZ-0003).",
      "statement": "req use of verification/Verified and validation/validated shall conform to their IEC 61508 / ISO 26262 meanings throughout the CLI, output, help and docs, such that no command outside the V&V evidence workflow names an unrelated operation with V&V vocabulary and the model well-formedness check is not named validate.",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [
        "illustrative"
      ],
