      "id": "SR-0010",
      "links": [
        {
          "kind": "Realizes",
          "target": "SF-0009"
        }
      ],
      "priority": "Must",
      "rationale": "Realizes SF-0009. A merge that silently keeps one side is a concrete materialization of HAZ-0001 (a safety requirement silently lost) that SF-0001's integrity hash cannot detect because the kept side is itself internally consistent.",
      "statement": "req merge shall perform a semantic three-way merge keyed by artifact id (and recursively by field), preserving every artifact present on either side unless it was deleted relative to the common ancestor. On any unresolvable divergence — the same artifact or field changed differently on both sides, or an edit-versus-delete — it shall preserve both sides and exit non-zero (a git conflict) rather than choosing one. The registered git merge driver must not suppress this exit status.",
      "status": "Verified",
      "tags": [],
      "tests": [
        {
          "actor": "Tom",
          "at": "2026-06-17T15:37:29.399766400Z",
